The HFDL decoder (built by default; comment out HFDL_INCLUDE in the Makefile to
omit it) links liquid-dsp (MIT) and includes a vendored copy of Phil Karn KA9Q's libfec
r=1/2 K=7 Viterbi decoder under hfdl_lib/libfec/, licensed under the GNU Lesser
General Public License (LGPL); see the license headers in those files. Its
signal-processing core, framing and protocol layers are ported from dumphfdl
(szpajder), which is GPL version 3 or later, and its ACARS block parser is
ported from libacars (szpajder, MIT); the HFDL build is therefore effectively
GPLv3, which this fork's "GPL v2 or later" permits. A build with HFDL omitted is
unaffected. hfdl_lib/hfdl_crc.c is dumphfdl's crc16_ccitt.
The embedded HFDL ground-station table in src/decode/hfdl_msg.c is a snapshot of
dumphfdl's etc/systable.conf.

The optional FreeDV 2020 receiver links Codec 2 (David Rowe, LGPL 2.1) and its
LPCNet FreeDV speech synthesizer (David Rowe, BSD 3-Clause). They are not vendored;
tools/build-freedv2020.sh builds pinned upstream revisions into build/freedv.
Their license texts and source are available from https://github.com/drowe67/codec2
and https://github.com/drowe67/LPCNet.

The VHF ACARS decoder (src/decode/acars_*.c, built by the same HFDL_INCLUDE flag
because it shares that decoder's message layer) has its MSK demodulator and
frame state machine ported from acarsdec (Thierry Leconte), which is licensed
under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2; see the license headers
in acarsdec's msk.c and acars.c. The LGPL permits this use in a GPL program.

The APT georeferencing includes the NORAD SGP4/SDP4 orbit propagator under
sgp4sdp4/, taken verbatim from gpredict's src/sgpsdp/ (Neoklis Kyriazis' C port
of T.S. Kelso's implementation of Spacetrack Report No. 3, plus Alexandru
Csete's modifications, GPL version 2 or later); see sgp4sdp4/1_COPYING and
sgp4sdp4/README-MACHPSDR. Its map overlay draws assets/coastline.bin, built by
tools/make_coastline.py from Natural Earth 1:50m coastline data, which is in the
public domain (naturalearthdata.com requires no permission, fee or attribution).

